{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790169738,"nonce":"ywrlxXCpcTHvsB5wqrpEEhQTTDQ=","title":"Haxe bridge loses cross-class plugin return types","message":"Removing the WindowHandle import and annotation from the window fixture makes WindowBuilder.open() infer Dynamic instead of window.WindowHandle. The plugin describe output carries the correct Object identity, but Bridge.haxeType only searches the current per-class module and namespaced language imports. Without a concrete return type, generated inline methods are reached through dynamic lookup and Ash aborts on a null pointer in std/src/obj.rs.\n\nReproduced without a GUI using Data.vector() returning Vec2 followed by vector.len(), with no Vec2 import or annotation. The bytecode compiled successfully and running it aborted with the same null-pointer panic.\n\nThe local fix indexes all plugin class identities before emitting signatures. The headless fixture now also checks an instance method returning a different class (Vec2.tally() -\u003e Tally), exercising both description orders without imports or annotations. The window fixture now infers WindowHandle and its bytecode has been rebuilt.","files":null}]}